## 7. Choosing the configuration

Three things were chosen on the validation era: the ridge variant (feature set and intercept), the decay `δ` and the sharpness `θ`. Choosing them on the judged window would let the reported number partly measure how many configurations I tried.

The validation origins run from {{val_first}} to {{val_last}} ({{val_n}} origins). The last target resolves on {{val_last_target}}. The chosen configuration is {{chosen_ridge_tag}}, δ = {{chosen_delta}} and θ = {{chosen_theta}}, with a validation RMSE of {{val_rmse_combo}} for the combination, against {{val_rmse_ar1}} for the AR(1) and {{val_rmse_rw}} for the random walk.

Those validation scores were used to pick the configuration, so they are not independent evidence about the combination. I report them for completeness.

The full grid of {{n_grid}} configurations is in [`data/processed/validation_metrics.json`](../data/processed/validation_metrics.json), along with every boosting trial. The best five:

