## 11. Other cuts and timing sensitivity

### Timing

Every non-spot predictor was pushed a further week late and the whole backtest, selection included, was rerun. Selection picked {{timing_extra_chosen_same}}.

{{table_timing}}

The AR(1) models and the random walk use spot only, so they do not move. Among the rest, the largest change outside gradient boosting is {{timing_max_other_change}}. Gradient boosting's RMSE changes by {{timing_gbm_change}} ({{timing_gbm_base}} to {{timing_gbm_extra}}), so a statement about its accuracy depends on the release-lag assumptions. The combination moves from {{timing_combo_base}} to {{timing_combo_extra}}.

### Other cuts

- Strict cut. Keeping only origins whose targets also fall inside 2025 ({{n_targets_in_2025}} origins), the combination scores {{strict_combo}}, the AR(1) {{strict_ar1_log}} and the random walk {{strict_rw}}. This is a subset of the same data. It is not an independent confirmation.
- Validation era. The combination scores {{val_rmse_combo}} and the AR(1) {{val_rmse_ar1}}, but that era chose the configuration (section 7).
- Determinism. The pipeline reruns from the committed raw files with no randomness beyond fixed seeds, and CI fails if the regenerated files under `data/processed`, the README or this document differ from what is committed.

